.TH NPROC 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
nproc \- print the number of available processing units
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nproc
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the number of processing units available to this process, via
Rust's own
.BR std::thread::available_parallelism .
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR and \fB\-\-version\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero if the count couldn't be determined.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lscpu (1),
.BR mitos\-box (1)
